Problem! Hero cards are all in ONE column (x=48) and stacked vertically: 吕布 y204, 亚瑟 y304, 铠 404... Each row is a separate full-width row → HFlowContainer is not wrapping into 3 columns; it's placing 1 card per line. Why? HFlowContainer width inside ScrollContainer: when horizontal scroll disabled, ScrollContainer child (hero_box) width may be its minimum width (236?) rather than scroll width. Actually hero_box is VBox inside ScrollContainer; VBox min width = max child min = flow min width. HFlowContainer min width = widest child width (236). ScrollContainer sizes child to max(min size, viewport) when horizontal scroll disabled? Apparently not here — maybe ScrollContainer sets child width to its minimum because horizontal_scroll_mode DISABLED means no h-scroll and child width = scroll width? Hmm but observed all cards x=48, meaning flow width ≤ 246 (one column). So hero_box width = 236? Interesting.

Wait the ScrollContainer viewport is 760 wide; hero_box is VBox child. VBox min width = flow min = 236. ScrollContainer with horizontal disabled sets child width = viewport width normally? Apparently Godot sets child size to max child min size only, and with horizontal scroll disabled it should fit width... Maybe because vertical scrollbar not needed and `horizontal_scroll_mode=DISABLED` means the child width equals its minimum, not the viewport? Let me recall: ScrollContainer with horizontal scroll disabled clamps child width to viewport width? In Godot docs: "If horizontal scroll is disabled, the child control's width is set to the ScrollContainer's width." I thought so. But observed 1 column means flow width ~236. Hmm, maybe hero_box's width is 236 because VBox doesn't expand horizontally (size_flags default FILL but not EXPAND; ScrollContainer only stretches child if child has expand flag?). Yes! ScrollContainer: child is sized to at least viewport size only if size flags expand? Actually in Godot 4, ScrollContainer sets child rect based on its combined minimum size and then, if the child has SIZE_EXPAND, expands it to container size. Hmm. Existing original code had flow inside hero_box inside hero_scroll with cards 150 wide and scroll 820: likely also one column? The original design might have suffered same issue? Maybe original cards were in a single column (150 wide) within 820 scroll — lots of empty space. That may be part of why current UI looks cramped.

Fix: set `hero_box.size_flags_horizontal = Control.SIZE_EXPAND_FILL`? For ScrollContainer, docs say child expands if it has expand flag. Let's test setting hero_box.size_flags_horizontal = SIZE_EXPAND_FILL and flow too. Actually ScrollContainer's layout: It sets child size to viewport if child's size_flags has EXPAND in that axis; otherwise child min. So set hero_box custom_minimum_size.x = 760? That would force width 760 (plus vertical scrollbar → overflow 14 maybe horizontal disabled clips). Better set hero_box.size_flags_horizontal = SIZE_EXPAND_FILL. Let's check Godot source behavior: ScrollContainer::_reposition_children:
```
Size2 minsize = c->get_combined_minimum_size();
Rect2 r = Rect2(-Size2(get_h_scroll(), get_v_scroll()), minsize);
if (c->get_h_size_flags().has_flag(SIZE_EXPAND)) {
    r.size.width = MAX(r.size.width, size.width);
}
if (c->get_v_size_flags().has_flag(SIZE_EXPAND)) {
    r.size.height = MAX(r.size.height, size.height);
}
...
```
Yes! So add size_flags_horizontal EXPAND_FILL to hero_box. Then hero_box width = scroll viewport width (760) (minus nothing? max(minsize, size.width) = 760). Then flow width = hero_box width 760 (VBox stretches children horizontally by default FILL). HFlow width 760 → 3 columns (3*236+2*10=728). Scrollbar when appears reduces viewport width to ~746 but child width remains 760 → cards slightly clipped at right? ScrollContainer child width = max(minsize, size.width) where size.width is the scroll container's full rect (including scrollbar?). The child area is width minus v scrollbar? In _reposition_children, `size` is the ScrollContainer's size; child rect width = 760; scrollbar overlays? V scrollbar reduces `h_scroll` area? The viewport clip is size minus scrollbar? I think ScrollContainer child width extends under scrollbar possibly causing last card partially hidden behind scrollbar. 3*236+20=728 leaves 32px right margin, scrollbar ~12-20 → last card right edge at 728 < 740 visible area. Fine.

Alternatively set hero_box.custom_minimum_size.x = 740 and expand. With expand it becomes max(740, 760)=760. fine.

Now also increase? For roles with 6 cards → 2 rows. Good.

Let's fix hero_box.size_flags_horizontal. Also check middle skill rows 214 height each (fills) fine; stats 2 cols. Preview fine.

Also check that the hero list content is scrollable: with 3 columns, total height much less; roles total:
战士 6 cards → 2 rows = 2*90+10=190; 法师 maybe 3; 刺客 3; 射手 3; 辅助 2? Total ~ 190+... likely fits within 1073 → no scroll needed, but scroll allowed. Good.

Summ cards: 2 columns properly. Good.

One more concern: hero cards all at x=48 means left column's hero list currently just one column; after fix it's 3 columns. Let me apply and re-probe.

Also potential: HFlowContainer in ScrollContainer with vertical expanding child height? VBox hero_box has size flags vertical? default fill no expand; ScrollContainer child height = minsize (content height) → fine (it scrolls if taller).

